.TH "PERCH-ALIAS-ADD" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-alias\-add \- add an alias or catch\-all
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch alias add [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Add an exact address alias, or use \-\-catch\-all with a domain to route all unmatched addresses at that domain to the account. The address must not already belong to another account.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-account <value>
account email
.TP
.B \-\-address <value>
alias address or domain
.TP
.B \-\-catch\-all
route all unmatched addresses at \-\-address
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch alias add \-\-account you@example.com \-\-address sales@example.com

perch alias add \-\-account you@example.com \-\-catch\-all \-\-address example.net
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-alias\fR(1)
